---
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
import revisions from '../data/sources.json';
import { gfaSource } from '../data/gfa-reference';
---
<Layout title="Sources and licensing" description="Revision, attribution and license details for the pTOS Programmer’s Reference Manual.">
  <header class="directory-head"><h1>Sources and Licensing</h1></header>
  <h2 class="prm-section-heading ruled">Historical material</h2>
  <p>Historical descriptions and bindings are adapted from <em>tos.hyp</em> by the original TOS Hypertext authors,
    maintainers, translators and contributors. See the original foreword by Rolf Kotzian and the notices maintained
    by Michael Bernstein and Gerhard Stoll. The historical text uses the GNU General Public License published with the upstream source.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/source/tos.hyp/anhang/hilfe.u">Upstream foreword and licensing notice</a></li>
    <li><a href="/source/tos.hyp/COPYING.GPL">GNU General Public License, version 2</a></li>
    <li><a href="/source/historical-report.json">Full UDO coverage and translation review</a></li>
    <li><a href="/source/import-report.json">Editorial review and changes for the pilot entries</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>The <a href="/historical/en/contents/">English</a> and <a href="/historical/de/contents/" hreflang="de">German</a>
    imports are built directly from the upstream UDO.
    Each page links to its original source file. The report identifies images linked upstream for license review and pages with automated English translation findings.
    The two reviewed GFA BASIC variable renames are applied to the English output.</p>
  <p><a href={`https://github.com/${revisions.tos.repo}/archive/${revisions.tos.revision}.tar.gz`}>Download the complete pinned UDO source</a></p>
  <h2 class="prm-section-heading ruled">GFA BASIC</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/gfa-basic/">GFA BASIC reference</a> cites <cite>{gfaSource.title}</cite>,
    credited to {gfaSource.originalAuthor} with the hypertext port by {gfaSource.portCredits}.
    Consult BAFO for the source. <a href={gfaSource.url}>{gfaSource.url}</a></p>
  <h2 class="prm-section-heading ruled">Pinned sources</h2>
  <ul class="source-revisions">
    {Object.values(revisions).map(({ repo, revision }) => <li><a href={`https://github.com/${repo}/tree/${revision}`}>{repo}</a> <code>{revision}</code></li>)}
  </ul>
  <p><a href={`https://github.com/${revisions.ptos.repo}/pull/${revisions.ptos.pullRequest}`}>pTOS PR #903</a> ·
    <a href={`https://github.com/${revisions.paratos.repo}/pull/${revisions.paratos.pullRequest}`}>ParaTOS PR #27</a></p>
  <p> <a href="https://github.com/kelihlodversson/ptos-docs">Manual source and revision history</a></p>
</Layout>
